<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed Subsumption Table</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table </span><a href="#A4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix D Detailed Subsumption Table ‣ M*: A Modular, Extensible, Serving Systemfor Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> expands the simplified comparison in
§</span><a href="#S3" title="3 The Walk Graph ‣ M*: A Modular, Extensible, Serving Systemfor Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (Table </span><a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3 The Walk Graph ‣ M*: A Modular, Extensible, Serving Systemfor Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">) along nine axes,
each tracing back to a primitive or capability introduced in
§</span><a href="#S3" title="3 The Walk Graph ‣ M*: A Modular, Extensible, Serving Systemfor Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="A4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>The Walk Graph compared with existing multimodal serving
abstractions. vLLM-Omni and SGLang-Omni implement stage graphs at
<em id="A4.T3.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">engine-instance</em> granularity; VoxServe specializes a single
<span id="A4.T3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Model</span> interface for SpeechLMs. Each prior system corresponds
to a restriction of the Walk Graph (see §<a href="#S3" title="3 The Walk Graph ‣ M*: A Modular, Extensible, Serving Systemfor Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</figcaption>
