<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="font-size:90%;">Model weights.</h4>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table </span><a href="#A9.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Model weights. ‣ Appendix I Artifact and Code Reproducibility Details ‣ M*: A Modular, Extensible, Serving Systemfor Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> lists pretrained checkpoints used in the
evaluation, with HuggingFace mirrors (or upstream URLs) and licenses.
Checkpoints are downloaded from these locations on first use; </span><span id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">M*</span><span id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
performs no further fine-tuning. The V-JEPA 2 AC checkpoint is the
encoder</span><math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">action-conditioned predictor bundle published on FAIR S3
(HuggingFace does not host an AC variant).</span></p>
</div>
